@startuml
title D7 — Customer Implementation Roadmap
caption Typical Surefyre implementation from kickoff through stabilization

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam activityBackgroundColor #F8FBFF
skinparam activityBorderColor #5B6B7A
skinparam activityFontColor #1F2933
skinparam activityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF4CC
skinparam activityDiamondBorderColor #A67C00
skinparam ArrowColor #4F6172

start

:1. Project Kickoff;

note right
  Confirm:
  - customer and stakeholders
  - implementation scope
  - project objectives
  - roles and responsibilities
  - schedule and milestones
end note

:2. Requirements Workshops;

note right
  Understand:
  - current business process
  - users and user roles
  - application forms
  - underwriting rules
  - integrations
  - migration requirements
end note

:3. Solution Design;

note right
  Define:
  - future-state workflow
  - form structure
  - fields and validation
  - routing and referrals
  - permissions
  - integration mappings
end note

:4. Configure Surefyre;

note right
  Configure:
  - form builder
  - JSON schema
  - HTML and JavaScript
  - workflow rules
  - notifications
  - calculations
end note

:5. Configure Integrations;

note right
  Support:
  - REST and SOAP APIs
  - endpoint configuration
  - authentication
  - field mappings
  - request and response testing
end note

:6. Prepare and Migrate Data;

note right
  Activities may include:
  - source-data analysis
  - data cleanup
  - Python transformations
  - import-file preparation
  - reconciliation
end note

:7. Execute Testing;

note right
  Testing includes:
  - functional testing
  - negative testing
  - integration testing
  - regression testing
  - migration validation
end note

:8. Business UAT;

if (UAT approved?) then (Yes)

  :9. Prepare Production Deployment;

  note right
    Confirm:
    - production configuration
    - permissions
    - endpoints
    - credentials
    - documentation
    - support readiness
  end note

  :10. Go Live;

  :11. Run Production Smoke Tests;

  :12. Stabilization and Hypercare;

  note right
    Support:
    - early production usage
    - issue reproduction
    - defect correction
    - user questions
    - operational handoff
  end note

  :13. Capture Lessons Learned;

  :14. Identify Reusable Patterns
  and Product Improvements;

else (No)

  :8A. Correct Configuration
  or Integration Defects;

  :8B. Retest;

  :8C. Repeat Business UAT;

  if (Retest approved?) then (Yes)
    :9. Prepare Production Deployment;
    :10. Go Live;
    :11. Run Production Smoke Tests;
    :12. Stabilization and Hypercare;
    :13. Capture Lessons Learned;
    :14. Identify Reusable Patterns
    and Product Improvements;
  else (No)
    :Return to Solution Design
    and Reassess the Approach;
  endif

endif

stop

legend bottom
|= Stage |= Main focus |
| Kickoff | Scope, stakeholders, roles and schedule |
| Requirements | Current process, forms, rules, users and integrations |
| Design | Future workflow and configuration approach |
| Configuration | Forms, JSON, JavaScript, workflow and calculations |
| Integration | APIs, authentication, mappings and error handling |
| Migration | Data transformation, import and reconciliation |
| Testing | Functional, negative, integration and regression validation |
| UAT | Business confirmation that the solution meets its needs |
| Deployment | Production configuration and operational readiness |
| Hypercare | Go-live support, troubleshooting and stabilization |
| Improvement | Lessons learned and reusable practices |
endlegend

@enduml